#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:1
msgid "Tuple functions"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:3
msgid ""
"The standard library defines the following functions for manipulating tuples:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:5
msgid "`tuple_reduce`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:7
msgid ""
"Applies a two-parameter function cumulatively across a tuple, in order to "
"reduce the tuple to a single value."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:19
msgid ""
"When the `initial:` named parameter is provided, its value will be used to "
"initialize the reduction operation, and will be the default value if the "
"tuple is empty."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:30
msgid ""
"If `initial` is not provided, when the tuple has exactly one entry, its "
"value will be returned; when the tuple is empty, an error will be raised."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:33
msgid "`tuple_map`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:35
msgid ""
"Applies a function to each entry in a tuple, returning a tuple. Aliases "
"defined in the tuple will be passed through to the output."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:38
msgid ""
"```prql\n"
"prql target:sql.duckdb\n"
"\n"
"from invoices\n"
"select (\n"
"  tuple_map (date.to_text \"%d/%m/%Y\") {\n"
"    rcv_txt = received_on,\n"
"    prc_txt = processed_on,\n"
"  }\n"
")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:50
msgid "`tuple_zip`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:52
msgid ""
"Combines two tuples into one tuple by aligning them in parallel and creating "
"tuples out of each aligned pair. This can be used in conjunction with "
"`tuple_map` and `tuple_reduce` in various ways:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:64
msgid "`tuple_uniq`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:66
msgid ""
"Iteratively deduplicates a tuple by alias (or, when an alias is not defined, "
"by its referenced column name). This can help to have more control over "
"situations when a column may be being overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:70
msgid ""
"For example, the following includes all columns from both `invoices` and "
"`shipments` in the final result, even those that have overlapping names:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:81
msgid ""
"Adding `select (tuple_uniq take:late {invoices.*, shipments.*})` will allow "
"the columns from `shipments` to appear in the output taking precedence over "
"those from `invoices`."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:94
msgid "Using `take:early` rather than `take:late` flips the priority."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:105
msgid "Items in a tuple without a name or an alias will be dropped."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:112
msgid "`tuple_reverse`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/stdlib/tuple.md:114
msgid "Reverses the order of a tuple."
msgstr ""
